# Requests for the TaskTracker API (Visual Studio / VS Code REST Client).
# 1. Start the API:  dotnet run --project src/TaskTracker.Api --launch-profile https
# 2. Set @password to your demo user's password locally. Do not commit a real password.
# 3. Run "login", copy accessToken into @token, then run the other requests.

@host = https://localhost:7061
@username = demo
@password = <your-demo-password>
@token = <paste-accessToken-here>

### Login
# @name login
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "{{username}}", "password": "{{password}}" }

### Current user (requires token)
GET {{host}}/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### List projects (anonymous)
GET {{host}}/api/projects

### Tasks for project 1 (anonymous)
GET {{host}}/api/projects/1/tasks

### Create a task (requires token)
POST {{host}}/api/projects/1/tasks
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": "Write release notes", "description": "Draft for v1", "dueDateUtc": "2026-12-01T00:00:00+08:00", "status": "Todo" }

### Update task status (requires token)
PATCH {{host}}/api/tasks/1/status
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "InProgress" }

### Mutation without a token -> 401
POST {{host}}/api/projects
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Should be rejected" }
